                            <Polygon POINTS="411 1944 409 1956 2175 1966 2179 1948 2177 1917 1772 1905 1770 1905 1558 1915 1529 1905 1527 1905 1525 1905 1523 1905 1484 1915 1406 1905 1404 1905 1347 1915 1273 1903 1271 1903 1226 1913 1204 1903 1202 1903 1200 1903 1122 1915 944 1915 910 1903 908 1903 906 1903 904 1903 871 1913 785 1903 783 1903 411 1911 411 1944"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="the Asiatic Eskimo the ceremonial of the winter is connected in most villages,"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_2-129_l26" HPOS="411" VPOS="1962" WIDTH="1772" HEIGHT="59" BASELINE="413 2007 2183 2003" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="413 2007 413 2021 2181 2017 2183 2003 2179 1974 2042 1962 2040 1962 1966 1972 1940 1962 1938 1962 1936 1962 1888 1972 1860 1962 1858 1962 1856 1962 1799 1972 1750 1962 1748 1962 1747 1962 1707 1972 1678 1962 1676 1962 1674 1962 1570 1972 1521 1962 1519 1962 1517 1962 1515 1962 1500 1974 1357 1974 1298 1962 1296 1962 1294 1962 1263 1972 1186 1964 1184 1964 1182 1964 1180 1964 1167 1974 1130 1964 1128 1964 1126 1964 1124 1964 1096 1974 889 1964 887 1964 885 1964 848 1974 634 1964 632 1964 630 1964 611 1974 548 1964 546 1964 411 1975 413 2007"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="not with Kereˊtkun, but with the Big-Woman. Some families in the villages"/>
                    </TextLine>

